# Antigravity Workspace Rules - n8n Project

## 1. Core Operating Principles
- **n8n Workflow Control**: Control and manage all n8n workflows strictly through the n8n Public API or n8n MCP tools.
- **Workflow Modifications**: When modifying or updating existing workflows, do NOT create new duplicates (POST). Instead, search for the workflow by name using `GET /api/v1/workflows`, and update it in-place using `PUT /api/v1/workflows/{id}`.
- **Node Schema Compliance**: Ensure generated workflow JSON strictly adheres to official n8n node schema specifications.
- **Environment Variables**: Always reference API keys, URLs, and sensitive credentials via `.env`. NEVER hardcode sensitive data in source files or node configs.

## 2. Git & Versioning Automation
- **Auto-Commit Trigger**: Automatically run `git add .` and `git commit` upon completing a logical unit of work.
- **Commit Message Specification**:
  - Format: `<type>: <short summary>`
  - Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`, `chore`.
  - Body Requirement: Write a 2-3 line detail in Korean explaining **what was changed** and **why/the goal of the change**.
- **CHANGELOG Maintenance**: Log every meaningful change, script addition, and integration result in `CHANGELOG.md` under the root directory with dates and version tags.
- **Remote Synchronization**: Automatically execute `git push origin main` after a successful commit.

## 3. Safety Guardrails (Essential for Turbo Mode)
- **Forbidden Git Commands**: NEVER run destructive actions such as `git push --force`, `git reset --hard`, or deleting git histories without explicit prompt confirmation.
- **Secret Protection**: Ensure `.env` or sensitive API keys are listed in `.gitignore` and NEVER staged/committed.

## 4. MCP & Workflow Technical Constraints
- **n8n MCP Server**: `https://kuro-factory.app.n8n.cloud/mcp-server/http`
- **Allowed Tools**: `n8n-mcp`
- **Apiframe & Suno Automation**:
  - Authenticate Apiframe API requests using `Authorization: Bearer <API_TOKEN>` sourced from `.env`.
  - Account for asynchronous task processing (handling task IDs, retry/polling loops, and response validation) when constructing Suno music generation nodes.

## 5. n8n Workflow & Credential Management Rules

### 1. Workflow Update Policy (수정 정책)
- **Do NOT create duplicate workflows**: When modifying an existing workflow, do NOT create a new workflow (`POST /workflows`).
- **Use Update Endpoint**: Search for the existing workflow by name or ID, then use `PUT /workflows/{id}` to apply changes within the same workflow.
- **Cleanup**: If duplicate workflows exist, leave only the most recent version and clean up inactive test workflows.

### 2. Registered Credentials Rules (등록된 자격 증명 사용 규칙)
When creating or updating nodes that require authentication, strictly use the pre-configured credentials below:

- **Google Drive**:
  - Type: `googleDriveOAuth2Api`
  - Name: `Google Drive API`
  - Rule: Must use native `n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive` node. Do NOT use standard HTTP Request node for Google Drive API.

- **Google Sheets**:
  - Type: `googleSheetsOAuth2Api`
  - Name: `Google Sheets account`
  - Rule: Must use native `n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets` node with `Google Sheets account` credential for all sheet operations (append, update).
  - Parameter Mapping Rule: 
    - **Operation**:
      - For reading rows (**`Get Row(s)`**), the `operation` parameter should be **omitted** entirely in the JSON parameters object. In n8n v4, omitting the operation parameter defaults it to "Get Row(s)". Do NOT write `"readRows"` or `"read"`, as this is treated as an invalid value in this version and hides the sheet configuration.
    - **Always Output Data**:
      - When reading sheets that may have only the header row and no data (empty sheet), always set `"alwaysOutputData": true` at the node's root level to prevent workflow errors when no data is returned.
    - **Document**: Always use **`By ID`** (`mode: "id"`) with the spreadsheet ID (do NOT use `By URL` to avoid URL parsing and sync errors).
    - **Sheet**: Use **`From List`** (or `By Name`) with the exact sheet tab name (e.g. `"시트1"`) to guarantee stable schema resolution.
  
- **Google Gemini**:
  - Type: `googlePalmApi` (or Google Gemini API)
  - Name: `Google Gemini API`
  - Rule: Must use `n8n-nodes-base.googleGemini` node or attach `Google Gemini API` credential.
  - Model Name Rule: When configuring the Chat Model (`@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGoogleGemini`), must explicitly specify `models/gemini-3.6-flash` (or the latest verified active model) as `modelName` because older versions (1.5/2.5) are deprecated or restricted for new API keys on the v1beta endpoint.

- **Telegram**:
  - Type: `telegramApi`
  - Name: `Telegram Bot API`
  - Rule: Use native `n8n-nodes-base.telegram` node with `Telegram Bot API` credential.

- **Apify**:
  - Type: None (Direct Bearer Header Auth)
  - Rule: Uses HTTP Request Node with custom header parameters. Must set `authentication` to `"none"`, enable `sendHeaders: true`, and add an `"Authorization"` header with the value `"Bearer <Token>"` sourced from `process.env.APIFY_API_KEY` (avoiding credential manager binding due to sync bugs).

- **Apiframe**:
  - Type: None (Direct Header Auth)
  - Rule: Uses HTTP Request Node with custom header parameters. Must set `authentication` to `"none"`, enable `sendHeaders: true`, and add a header named `"X-API-Key"` with the value sourced from `process.env.APIFRAME_API_KEY` (avoiding credential manager binding due to sync bugs).

- **Tavily**:
  - Type: `httpHeaderAuth` (or `tavilyApi`)
  - Name: `Tavily API`
  - Rule: When using HTTP Request node, set `authentication` to `"genericCredentialType"` and `genericAuthType` to `"httpHeaderAuth"` (do NOT use `"generic"`). If using native Tavily node, ensure `tavilyApi` credential is mapped correctly.

### 3. Node Configuration Guardrails
- **Execution Method Check**: Ensure all native nodes have valid `resource` and `operation` fields filled in to prevent `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'execute')` errors.
- **Credential Binding**: Every API node must explicitly bind its corresponding credential from the list above.
- **If Node Condition Typing**: In n8n v2 If nodes (`n8n-nodes-base.if`), the `"operator"` field inside each object of the `"conditions"` array must be defined as an object rather than a string.
  - For Boolean checks: `"operator": { "type": "boolean", "operation": "true", "singleValue": true }`
  - For Number checks: `"operator": { "type": "number", "operation": "smaller" }` (e.g. for less-than comparisons)
  Omitting this object structure and writing string operators (e.g. `"isTrue"`, `"lt"`) triggers a schema processing crash (`Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'toLowerCase')`).
- **Connection Input Port Indexing**: In n8n workflow JSON, the `index` property in the connection target object represents the **input port index of the target node**. For almost all standard nodes (including If and Telegram nodes), they have only a single input port, so the target `index` MUST be `0`. Setting target `index` to `1` (or anything else) routes the connection to a non-existent second input, preventing n8n from matching incoming data with the node's parameters, causing conditions/parameters to be ignored or display as empty in the UI.
- **Node-Level Retry Settings**: To configure "Retry on Fail" on individual nodes in n8n workflow JSON, the settings must be set directly at the root of the node object using the properties `"retryOnFail": true`, `"maxTries": <Number>`, and `"waitBetweenTries": <Milliseconds>` (e.g. `5000` for 5 seconds). Using `"onError": "retry"` is invalid and will be ignored by n8n.
- **Expression Evaluation Prefix (=)**: Any node parameter in n8n JSON that contains variable expressions (like `{{ $json.body }}` or `{{ $json.text }}`) must be prefixed with an `=` character (e.g. `prompt: "=..."` or `text: "=..."`). If the `=` prefix is omitted, n8n treats the entire value as a static string, causing the raw `{{ ... }}` placeholders to be sent literally to the LLM or external APIs, resulting in "empty data" or evaluation failures.

## 6. Agent Skills Guidelines
This project has 5 dedicated skills defined in `.agents/skills/`. Apply the following skill rules for each task request:
1. **For research and planning requests:** Refer to the guidelines and structure of the `content-research-writer` skill.
2. **When blog visuals / SVG / thumbnails are needed:** Generate code/design referring to the `canvas-design` skill.
3. **When writing image prompts:** Apply the prompt expansion rules of the `image-enhancer` skill.
4. **When analyzing video data and subtitle structures:** Refer to the guidelines of the `video-downloader` skill.
5. **When reviewing design/tone & manner:** Reflect the consistency guidelines of the `brand-guidelines` skill.

## 7. Localization & Translation Workflow Rules (국제화 및 영문 최적화 규칙)
- **Agent Reasoning & Processing (에이전트 추론)**: When the user communicates in Korean, the agent should internally process the reasoning, file searches, and technical tasks in English to maximize precision, but must always present the final responses and walkthroughs in natural Korean.
- **Node Prompts (노드 프롬프트)**: Write all system and planning prompts in n8n LLM nodes in English to ensure high instruction compliance. Add explicit instructions at the end of the prompt to output the final user-facing text (script, notifications) in natural Korean.
- **Comments & Annotations (한글 주석)**: To ensure readability for the user, always include clear Korean comments or description fields inside the node parameters and JS code blocks explaining what the English prompts or code blocks do.

## 8. Token & API Cost Optimization Guardrails (토큰 및 API 비용 최적화 가이드라인)
- **Multi-Item Execution Guard (다중 실행 방지)**: Nodes retrieving lists or database rows (e.g. Google Sheets read) must be consolidated into a single item via Code nodes before passing to downstream API or LLM nodes to prevent runaway batch executions.
- **LLM Retry Limits (AI 노드 재시도 제약)**: Set `maxTries` to at most **3** (instead of 10) on LLM/HTTP nodes to prevent infinite billing loops during prolonged API outages or rate-limiting.
- **Loop Circuit Breakers (반복 루프 안전 차단기)**: Every programmatic loop (e.g. rewrite retries) must enforce a strict execution count ceiling (e.g., maximum of 2 retries per content item) to prevent infinite loops.
- **State Caching & Reuse (데이터 캐싱 및 재사용)**: Downstream loops must reuse cached intermediate data (e.g., raw Tavily search logs saved in Google Sheets) instead of calling fresh external search engines or LLM research steps repeatedly.